  "name": "Bering's Voyages; Volume 2",
  "description": "An account of the efforts of the Russians to determine the relation of Asia and America. (Two volumes) Steller's Journal of the sea voyage from Kamchatka to America and return on the second expedition from 1741 - 1742. [Reference: Golder, F.A. 1925. Bering's Voyages: Volume II. American Geographical Society, Research Series No. 1, American Geographical Society, Broadway at 156th Street, New York. pp. 291.] This volume may be found at many university libraries.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To record the voyages and finding of Vitus Bering.",
